  "body": "LOT-133\nCloses #223\nClaim: cloud/lot-133-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/lot-133-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (id on its first verdict, below)\n\n## What and why\n**Problem.** The Plus entry \"Alertes Qualitay\" opened a placeholder, and legacy's new-AQ count (GAP-005) was missing from the Plus tab, the row and the iPad sidebar, including on a first logged-out launch (operator, #223, 2026-11-11).\n\n**Cause.** The LOT-055 client existed but no app code used it: no feed model, no screen, no stored last check, no AQ address in the build.\n\n**Change** (spec: `docs/lots/LOT-133-aq-feed-badge.md`):\n- `QualityAlertsModel` (`@Observable @MainActor`): count of items published at or after `last_check_aq`, category 25 removed **before** counting by the Q-7 rule (`ForumVisibility`), a ticket so a count already in flight cannot bring the badge back once the list was shown (no phantom badge), a failed answer keeps the count, the list marks itself seen only after its rows are set.\n- `QualityAlertsView`: rows open the reader on `ReaderTarget(link:)`, so page and anchor are kept (#105, #106); failure keeps rows and offers a retry.\n- Plus tab, Plus row and iPad sidebar badges; the count is read 3 s after the root appears, logged out too.\n- `SettingKey.aqLastCheck` (`last_check_aq`, device scope); `AQ_BASE_URL` → `AQBaseURL` in `App/Config` (ADR 0007). The committed value is the public host legacy hard-codes, so a build without `Secrets.xcconfig` shows the badge: **operator to confirm**.\n- No wider: no Home AQ section (LOT-144), no create flow (LOT-134), no entity decoding of titles (legacy shows them undecoded, B4).\n\n## How it was verified\n- `SettingKeyTests.aqLastCheck…` (fails to compile without the key) and the two catalogue tests that pin every key (`SettingKeyTests`, `SettingScopeTests`); `swift test` on `HFRKit`: 2048 tests pass.\n- App tests (`App/SwiftHFRTests/QualityAlerts/`, `RootAlertsBadgeTests`) run over the captured feed `T01` parsed by the real `AQFeedParser`; no AQ answer is written by hand. The model, its source and `ReaderTarget` do not import UIKit or SwiftUI, so they were compiled and tested on Linux in a scratch package: 19 tests pass. Eight mutations each fail a test: no ticket in `load`, no last-check write, no badge reset, no category filter, no load-ticket guard, count ignoring the last check, a failure that marks seen, no ticket check in the count.\n- SwiftLint run locally on every changed Swift file: clean.\n- **Not run by the author** (Linux cannot build the app): the views, the Plus integration and the app test target, hence `compile-check`. Device checks owed, for the list on #893: light, dark, Dynamic Type XL, iPhone and iPad (tab badge, sidebar badge, reader opening at the anchor).\n- **Pending captures** (one Mac capture issue): a feed answer holding a category-25 item (`T01` has none: the visibility tests derive one from a captured item by changing its `cat`, and say so); an item whose reporter comment holds an entity (#438).\n\n## Checklist (AGENTS.md §9)\n- [x] Module boundaries respected (no sibling imports in HFRKit, no UI framework in HFRKit)\n- [x] Tests added/updated — differential tests for ported logic\n- [x] No secrets; fixtures anonymized (`T01` is the committed capture)\n- [x] Docs updated (lot spec, App/README); the issue is closed by hand after the merge\n- [x] Author model: Sonnet 5.5 / Reviewer model: Opus 5.5 (must differ)\n- [x] Changes a gap row: `### Ledger` below\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-005\nSwiftHFR final: Le badge du Plus, de la ligne « Alertes Qualitay » et de la barre latérale iPad compte les AQ plus récentes que la dernière visite de la liste (catégorie 25 retirée avant de compter, comme pour le forum), relu 3 s après l'ouverture même déconnecté et à chaque nouvelle session; la liste ouvre le message à sa page et à son ancre.\n```\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJJFWq7RZzreRt7ZxU)_",
